description:
Barcelona, Catalonia, Spain | Human Resources | Full-time | Hybrid

**Country HR Manager (M/F)**
============================

At **Datawords** (part of the **87seconds Group**), we believe that every culture and every context deserves a unique approach. That is why we strive to help our clients understand and embrace differences, needs and traditions.

Every day, we empower brands to connect with anyone, anywhere in the world, while respecting the unique characteristics of each individual. Our 1,000 employees across 25 countries combine human intelligence with artificial intelligence to create, deploy and manage an infinite variety of content that resonates authentically and emotionally across more than 160 cultures.

Leading global brands such as Henkel, L'Oréal, LVMH, Carrefour and Michelin have trusted us for many years to support their international ambitions.

**About the job**
-----------------

To support our business and ensure continuity within our HR team, Datawords is looking for a:

**Country HR Manager (M/F) – 6-month fixed-term contract**

Based in Barcelona, Spain, within an office of approximately 70 employees, you will lead the local HR function, reporting to the local General Manager and to the Global HR Director based in Paris.

As the main HR contact for the Spanish entity, you will be responsible for all aspects of HR management, combining operational HR responsibilities, employee relations and office management.

You will act as a key business partner to the local General Manager, supporting the implementation of the Group's global HR strategy at local level, while ensuring its alignment with local business priorities and Spanish labour regulations.

In a fast-evolving business environment, you will contribute to organisational development, support change initiatives and help managers address their HR challenges.

**Management:** Manage and support one HR Generalist.

**Your main responsibilities will include:**

### **HR Operations & Administration**

* Oversee all HR administrative activities throughout the employee lifecycle, including recruitment administration, onboarding, employment contracts and amendments, employee records, absences, leave management, offboarding and all related HR documentation;
* Ensure the accurate and timely execution of payroll in collaboration with an external payroll provider, including the collection and verification of payroll data and the follow-up of payroll-related matters;
* Ensure compliance with Spanish labour law, social security regulations and the applicable collective bargaining agreement (*Convenio Colectivo*);
* Manage employee relations and provide guidance to managers and employees on HR policies, procedures and employment-related matters;
* Handle disciplinary matters, including investigations, disciplinary procedures and employee relations issues, in compliance with local labour legislation.

### **Employee Relations & Social Dialogue**

* Manage relations with employee representatives and relevant employee representative bodies, ensuring constructive social dialogue;
* Prepare and participate in meetings with employee representatives, ensuring compliance with local legal requirements and internal policies;
* Contribute to maintaining a positive working environment and fostering employee engagement.

### **Talent & HR Management**

* Act as a key HR business partner to the local General Manager, supporting the translation and implementation of the Group's global HR strategy into local HR priorities and initiatives;
* Provide HR guidance and support to managers throughout the employee lifecycle, including recruitment, onboarding, performance reviews, compensation, talent management, employee development, conflict resolution and departures;
* Manage the local recruitment process in close collaboration with hiring managers and the Group HR team;
* Support organisational changes and act as a proactive change agent, ensuring alignment with the Group's culture and business objectives;
* Coordinate and implement the Group's annual HR campaigns, including performance management, talent reviews, succession planning and compensation reviews;
* Foster the Group's culture and roll out global HR initiatives locally, including talent management projects and HRIS implementation;
* Ensure appropriate HR policies, processes and tools are implemented and adapted to the local context;
* Develop a strong understanding of the business, its activities and operational challenges in order to anticipate HR needs and provide relevant, pragmatic HR support.

### **Office Management**

* Oversee office management activities, ensuring the smooth day-to-day running of the Barcelona office;
* Supervise and support the HR Assistant in their HR and office management responsibilities;
* Ensure employees benefit from a pleasant, efficient and well-organised working environment.

**Qualifications**
------------------

* Master's degree in Human Resources Management or equivalent;
* Minimum of **3 years of solid experience** in an HR Generalist, HR Manager or HR Business Partner role, ideally in an international and multicultural environment;
* Strong knowledge of Spanish labour law, social security regulations and collective bargaining agreements;
* Proven experience in payroll management and HR administration;
* Experience managing employee relations and working with employee representative bodies;
* Experience handling disciplinary procedures and employment-related matters;
* Previous experience in office management would be an advantage;
* Ability to work closely with senior management and provide sound HR advice on employee and organisational matters;
* Strong business acumen and genuine curiosity to understand the company's activities, business challenges and operational priorities;
* Ability to translate business needs into relevant HR actions and to support organisational changes in a fast-evolving environment;
* Strong organisational skills, autonomy and a hands-on approach;
* Excellent interpersonal and communication skills;
* Fluent in English. Spanish is essential.

**Conditions**
--------------

* **Location:** Barcelona, Spain;
* **Contract type:** Temporary replacement contract (*contrato de sustitución*) to ensure continuity of the HR function during the current HR Manager's temporary absence, with the possibility of a subsequent replacement period covering maternity leave, subject to applicable Spanish labour law;
* **Start date:** As soon as possible;
* **Working hours:** Full-time, 40 hours per week;

*We believe that diversity and inclusion are essential to the success of our company. We are committed to creating an inclusive working environment where every employee, regardless of their background or abilities, can flourish.*

*Datawords guarantees equal opportunities throughout the recruitment process, regardless of gender, ethnic origin, religion, sexual orientation, social background, disability or age.*
